gs-native-pc (patch 74): a coalesced primitive run compares its draw state once instead of once per primitive

Patch 66 turns per-primitive submits into same-state runs on the GS frontend, but the worker still receives each
primitive through the generic SubmitRun loop, which calls Submit() per primitive. Submit() compares the batch state
with the pending state field by field (`sameState`) on every primitive even though a run carries exactly one state.

Measured on the Asia disc at 0.5x (`GOW_GS_COST=1`, 5 s windows): `compare_ms` falls from 53-134 ms to 2-7 ms per
window and the per-primitive cost from ~250-260 ns to ~200-215 ns (ship deck, t=15-60 s). The comparison is not
removed, only amortized: the first primitive of the run still runs the full compare and flushes when it differs, so
the pending-batch contents are identical to the old path.

PS2X_GS_RUN_STATE_FAST=0 restores the per-primitive loop (the old behaviour) for A/B.

